# Local configuration, names only. Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill in what you have.
# `npm run dev:all` loads the repo-root `.env` for the gateway and the dashboard server.
# Every variable below is OPTIONAL: with none set, the sample tour (synthetic "Lumen Vale") works.
# Lines starting with "# NAME=" are off by default; remove the "# " to turn one on. Never commit real values.

# ---- Level 2: live Qloo data --------------------------------------------------------------
# Qloo hackathon API key. Without it: live runs are disabled; the sample tour still works.
# Also needs the harness: npm i -g @qloo/qloo-harness@^0.1.26 && qloo setup --qloo
# QLOO_API_KEY=
# Override the Qloo endpoint the harness uses (and the URL it is allowed to send credentials to; both must match).
# QLOO_BASE_URL=
# QLOO_TRUSTED_BASE_URL=
# Path of the harness binary if `qloo` is not on PATH (default: qloo).
# QLOO_BIN=
# Daily Qloo call ceilings (gateway-wide, and for the public MCP sessions). Defaults 2000 and 400.
# QLOO_DAILY_CEILING=
# QLOO_PUBLIC_DAILY_CEILING=
# Days a cached Qloo answer stays fresh (in-memory cache; lost on restart).
# QLOO_CACHE_TTL_DAYS=

# ---- Level 3: Gemini (narration, local acts, sponsor check, strategist) ---------------------
# Google AI Studio key (https://aistudio.google.com/apikey). Wins over Vertex when both are set.
# Without any Gemini credentials: those features are off and deterministic fallbacks run.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Force a backend: aistudio or vertex. Default: AI Studio if GEMINI_API_KEY is set, else Vertex if GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT is set.
# GEMINI_PROVIDER=
# Vertex AI instead of AI Studio: needs a project plus Google application-default credentials
# (gcloud auth application-default login). Also required for BigQuery analytics and Firestore.
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=
# GCP_PROJECT=
# Model names (defaults are set in code) and the Gemini daily cap (default 300).
# GEMINI_MODEL=
# GEMINI_FALLBACK_MODEL=
# GEMINI_DAILY_CEILING=

# ---- Optional extras ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tavily web search for "this week" and Advance & risks. Without it those two cards are off.
# TAVILY_API_KEY=
# BigQuery analytics. Off unless BOTH are set (and GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT + ADC). Tables: cloud_run/qloo_gateway/scripts/bq_setup.sh
# BQ_DATASET=
# BQ_LOCATION=

# ---- Storage (gateway) -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default is in-memory for cache, usage counts and team workspaces: no Firestore or ADC needed (dev:all forces memory).
# Set to firestore only on Google Cloud; it needs ADC.
# QLOO_CACHE_BACKEND=memory
# QLOO_USAGE_BACKEND=memory

# ---- Ports and wiring --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gateway port (default 8080 for the gateway, 8787 for the dashboard server; Vite is 5173).
# PORT=
# dev:all only: gateway port the dashboard server follows (default 8080).
# GATEWAY_PORT=
# Dashboard server -> gateway URL. dev:all sets http://127.0.0.1:8080. A loopback URL sends no Google identity token.
# QLOO_GATEWAY_URL=
# Directory holding showcase.json and backtest.json (the real recorded example). It is private under Qloo's
# data terms and not in this repo; without it the synthetic Lumen Vale sample is used.
# RECORDINGS_DIR=
# Private GCS bucket holding the same recordings (Cloud Run only).
# RECORDINGS_BUCKET=

# ---- Legacy and deployment-only (not needed for a local run) ----------------------------------------
# Original hackathon services; unset means their routes answer 503.
# TOUR_DATA_API_URL=
# DELIGHT_RENDERER_URL=
# ORCHESTRATOR_JOB_URL=
# Python MCP server: 1 = public demo mode (nine tools, rate limited).
# MCP_PUBLIC=
# Dev/test only: send team-workspace routes to a local in-memory server (node dist/collab/devServer.js).
# COLLAB_FAKE=
# COLLAB_FAKE_URL=
